speechtext:
They cannot understand how the federal government could have made the number of errors it made; blowing up the natural breakwater and now finding that they need a new breakwater; putting one back;

creating a scale model in order to learn what the people in the area could have told them a long time ago. If these statements are not true then I should be glad to hear about it from the minister, but they have been repeated over and over again to me by people in Newfoundland. To them it is almost unbelievable that so many mistakes could have been made by one group of people on one project.
Now almost a year has passed since we were here last year and were unable to get the story of why this breakwater was demolished and this new breakwater had to be built, perhaps the minister at long last can give us the whole story. Perhaps I am wrong. I am simply repeating what I have heard over and over again in Newfoundland from Newfoundlanders. They would be interested to hear that this story which they tell is not true. I ask the minister to bring us up to date on the last chapter of this very sorry story. I shall be very interested in what he has to say.
